  "intervention": "Four profiles: baseline, motion only, timing only, both. Motion adds current speed/actual steering/yaw/held native input plus existing pedal road-lateral velocity to wheel facts. Timing adds known post-response wait(0 or1s),60Hz and descriptive units stating inference is additional/variable/unknown for current reply. Only wheel factual packets change; full pedal question/rules/native menus identical. Gate geometry disabled throughout. Both active racers share assigned profile/wait. No future pose, action rules, advice, projection, repair, refreshed observation, retry or fallback.",
  "fixed": "Python60Hz dynamics,24m road,12m/s,.12rad wheel,1m footprint, contacts/rescue/phase/gate mechanics, goal-only race objective, action menus and native inverse. Both active drivers use same profile/delay. Episode goal is not supplied to the model.",
  "selection": "Exact0082state files reused byte-for-byte; no new state selection. Prior physical evidence: Outward drift:0080 blue tick199,5.714m body clearance,8.396m/s outward velocity,44.40deg heading error; earlier0081tick175 had8.876m clearance. Post-contact:0078race9 red tick720,one second after contacttick660,36.04deg heading error,8.659m clearance,4.893m/s outward velocity. Initialfeature scans and all failedguide/enumeration screens are retained. Selected before any new paid reply. Five new credits required because held-input post-contact controls pass three before later rescue. Simple1.2sguide failed both; retained native-input witnesses establish feasibility, including a bounded offlinebeam search for drift. No witness or search is available to paid collection or prompt.",
  "free_requirements": "Current complete full clock gate on this boot/server/source; all16 unique state/profile/delay exact native-interface controls with strict physics/timing/accounting audits. Free controller outcome credited/rescued/deadline is an ordinary task result; qualification does not require guide success. Separate offline native-input witnesses establish legal recovery at200ms and1200ms response cadences in each state. Preserve all free candidate failures.",
  "stop": "One actual process per explicit root admission, observed exit and full root plus wire/reservation review before next. Stop on native/provider/clock/accounting error; no retry or replacement. Rescue/deadline ordinary task outcomes. No other models, seeds or tuning.",
  "limits": "Three previous failure strata have two repeats/profile, normal post-contact one check/profile. Two selected recorded states, one track family, not a general reliability estimate. Pedal head remains unchanged and does not receive new timing information; this isolates wheel-question observability. Native latency varies; only extra wait is known. Motion/timing additions are supplied measurements/mechanics, not action advice. Existing solo motion benefits did not repeat, so no benefit is assumed. Physics/runtime/UI unchanged; all new factual flags default off."
